ESCAPE CONFIDENCE, registered in experiments/prereg_escape_confidence.json (sha256 43b8ee81ffb8..., frozen before any unmasked top-2 existed). Six cells, 3471 shared probe sources. The quantity is top-1 minus top-2 of the UNMASKED distribution -- the thing that actually flips -- not the stored margin, which measures leaving rather than choosing and was refused in the prereg.  THE FLOOR ACROSS THE LADDER (pythia-410m fp32 vs bf16, identical weights): tau=0.0 0.7089 (n=3463); tau=0.1 0.8195 (n=2615); tau=0.5 0.995 (n=1205); tau=1.0 0.9983 (n=593); tau=2.0 1.0 (n=166, NOT DECIDABLE).  KB does not fire: the floor rises from 0.7089 to 1.0 across the ladder, so the flips are substantially near-ties.  THE DECISIVE PAIR: tau=0.0 0.6355 (n=3462); tau=0.1 0.728 (n=2526); tau=0.5 0.9412 (n=1038); tau=1.0 0.9981 (n=521); tau=2.0 1.0 (n=157, NOT DECIDABLE).  far vs mamba-370m-hf: 0.0:0.3493; 0.1:0.3995; 0.5:0.6254; 1.0:0.8315; 2.0:0.9697.  far vs rwkv-4-430m-pile: 0.0:0.3393; 0.1:0.3801; 0.5:0.587; 1.0:0.8232; 2.0:0.9574.  far vs gpt-neo-125m: 0.0:0.3902; 0.1:0.4442; 0.5:0.6784; 1.0:0.9124; 2.0:1.0.  KD, registered because it is the tempting half-report: decisive-minus-far separation is 0.2759 at tau=0 and 0.1424 at the primary tau=1.0. IT DEGRADES -- the threshold buys precision at the cost of discrimination, and the floor improvement may not be quoted without this.  KC: modal-destination share among survivors is reported at every rung, so a rising agreement that is really a concentration onto one destination is visible.  REFUSALS: no p-value; no adjustment of the ladder or the 500-source floor; no claim that this makes the estimand quantization-robust -- bfloat16 is a far smaller perturbation and that test remains OWED; no semantic reading of any destination. THE PRIOR-ART RE-CHECK IS OWED AND BLOCKS WRITE-UP.

